      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "raw_response": "The scientific figure consists of four panels labeled a, b, c, and d, each depicting different aspects of magnetization behavior under varying conditions.\n\n**Panel a:**\n- **Axes:** \n  - X-axis: Temperature (T) in Kelvin (K), ranging from 0 to 400 K.\n  - Y-axis: Magnetization (M) in emu/g, ranging from 0.0 to 1.2 emu/g.\n- **Data Lines:**\n  - Red circles represent the Field-Cooled (FC) magnetization at H = 50 Oe.\n  - Blue diamonds represent the Zero-Field-Cooled (ZFC) magnetization at H = 50 Oe.\n- **Legend:** Indicates FC and ZFC with corresponding symbols and H = 50 Oe.\n- **Inset:** Shows the Curie temperature (T_C) with two values: T_C = 367 K and T_C = 778 K.\n\n**Panel b:**\n- **Axes:** \n  - X-axis: Temperature (T) in Kelvin (K), ranging from 0 to 900 K.\n  - Y-axis: Magnetization (M) in emu/g, ranging from 0.0 to 1.2 emu/g.\n- **Data Lines:**\n  - Red circles represent the Field-Cooled (FC) magnetization at H = 50 Oe.\n  - Blue diamonds represent the Zero-Field-Cooled (ZFC) magnetization at H = 50 Oe.\n- **Legend:** Indicates FC and ZFC with corresponding symbols and H = 50 Oe.\n- **Inset:** Shows the derivative of magnetization with respect to temperature (dM/dT) in emu/(g·K), ranging from -0.0001 to 0.0001 emu/(g·K). The inset also displays the Curie temperature (T_C) with two values: T_C = 367 K and T_C = 778 K.\n\n**Panel c:**\n- **Axes:** \n  - X-axis: Magnetic field (H) in kOe, ranging from -30 to 30 kOe.\n  - Y-axis: Magnetization (M) in emu/g, ranging from -20 to 20 emu/g.\n- **Data Lines:**\n  - Different temperatures are represented by various symbols and colors:\n    - 2 K (blue circles)\n    - 77 K (purple squares)\n    - 300 K (green diamonds)\n    - 400 K (red triangles)\n- **Pressure Condition:** p = 0 GPa.\n- **Legend:** Indicates the temperature conditions for each data line.\n\n**Panel d:**\n- **Axes:** \n  - X-axis: Magnetic field (H) in kOe, ranging from -30 to 30 kOe.\n  - Y-axis: Magnetization (M) in emu/g, ranging from -20 to 20 emu/g.\n- **Data Lines:**\n  - Different temperatures are represented by various symbols and colors:\n    - 2 K (blue circles)\n    - 77 K (purple squares)\n    - 300 K (green diamonds)\n    - 400 K (red triangles)\n- **Pressure Condition:** p = 1 GPa.\n- **Legend:** Indicates the temperature conditions for each data line.\n\nThe figure compares the magnetization behavior of a composite material and a composite High-Pressure Torsion (HPT) material under zero and 1 GPa pressure conditions, focusing on temperature and field dependencies.",
